<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17258" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ex-stĭmŭlo</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ext-</span></b> ), āvi,
			ātum, 1, v. a., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to prick up</i>, <i>to
				goad</i> (<b>poet.</b> and in post-Aug.
			prose). * </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aculeo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					9, 37, 61, § 132</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>to goad on</i>, <i>excite</i>, <i>instigate</i>, <i>stimulate</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aliquem dictis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. F.
					6, 588</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">corda furore bellandi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil. 1,
					38</span></i>
			; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">armentum libidinis furiis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					6, 27, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tigrim fame,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					5, 165</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">animum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac.
					A. 15, 50</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">libidinem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					8, 11, 8</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fata cessantia,</span>”
				i. e. <i>to hasten death</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					Tr. 3, 2, 29</span></i>
			. —<i>Pass.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">exstimulatur a libertis, ut ostenderet,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. A.
					4, 59</span></i>
			.</div>
